","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/74690","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74690","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74690.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74690.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-22T08:23:07Z"},"body":"### Why\r\n\r\n- When Airflow wants a running task to stop, for example after a user marks the task instance as failed, the supervisor sends the task's process SIGTERM. If the process is still running after `[core] killed_task_cleanup_time` seconds, the supervisor sends SIGKILL. The Go and TypeScript SDKs pass that SIGTERM to the task through its context, so the task can stop work it started, such as a job in an external system.\r\n\r\n### How\r\n\r\n- While a task runs, the SDK replaces the JVM's SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers through `sun.misc.Signal`. It puts the old handlers back after the supervisor has acknowledged the task's result.\r\n- `Context.isCancelled()` and `Context.awaitCancellation(Duration)` tell a task that Airflow asked it to stop.\r\n\r\n <!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\r\n      https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 -->\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nThank you for contributing!\r\n\r\nPlease provide above a brief description of the changes made in this pull request.\r\nWrite a good git commit message following this guide: https://chris.beams.io/posts/git-commit/\r\n\r\nPlease make sure that your code changes are covered with tests.\r\nAnd in case of new features or big changes remember to adjust the documentation.\r\n\r\nFor user-facing UI changes, please attach before/after screenshots (or a short\r\nscreen recording) so reviewers can assess the visual impact.\r\n\r\nFeel free to ping (in general) for the review if you do not see reaction for a few days\r\n(72 Hours is the minimum reaction time you can expect from volunteers) - we sometimes miss notifications.\r\n\r\nIn case of an existing issue, reference it using one of the following:\r\n\r\n* closes: #ISSUE\r\n* related: #ISSUE\r\n-->\r\ncloses: #72680\r\n---\r\n\r\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nIf generative AI tooling has been used in the process of authoring this PR, please\r\nchange below checkbox to `[X]` followed by the name of the tool, uncomment the \"Generated-by\".\r\n-->\r\n\r\n- [X] Yes - Claude Code\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nGenerated-by: [Tool Name] following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\r\n-->\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/74690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/74690/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":33929037837,"node_id":"CE_lADOAgUK288AAAABQMzxf88AAAAH5lQIDQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/33929037837","actor":{"login":"jason810496","id":68415893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NDE1ODkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68415893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496","html_url":"https://github.com/jason810496","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jason810496/repos","events_url"